OL,3,GNEWSAVeteran 'overwhelmed' by help
OL,4,Aafter arson attack
OL,5,
OL,6,FA disabled veteran whose fence and bins
OL,7,Fwere destroyed in an arson attack says
OL,8,Fhe has been "overwhelmed" by the
OL,9,Fresponse from the community.
OL,11,FMichael Howie, from Gloucester, said he
OL,12,Fwas facing the expense of replacing his
OL,13,Ffence as well as a #50 charge from the
OL,14,Fcouncil to replace his bins.
OL,16,FBut after contacting his local
OL,17,Fcouncillor and posting an appeal on
OL,18,FFacebook, the work has been carried out
OL,19,Ffor free by a local builder and new
OL,20,Fbins delivered free-of-charge by the
OL,21,Fcouncil.
OL,23,APub: 12-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
